# Round 18, C1-18 (follows). L §4.6 step 5, Outside a lifespan: "where ... d lies outside its lifespan (for an input
# keyed by one period index, the first day of its key's period, as in step 1), a read with no candidate is none".
# bolt ends 2026-02-28 and salary has no March row: salary[bolt, 2026-03] is none at any law date (April, February)
# and with none (q2); February's row is read at an April law date (step 1: the key is the value's valid time).
=== m.tally
model m
  tally 2
  on 2026-12-31
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31
source s "s"
unit PLN: currency minor 0.01
kind jobs
input salary[j in jobs, m in months]: money PLN
def sal_at[j in jobs, m in months, d in days]: money PLN = salary[j, m] at d
version v
  cite s
  governs 2026-01..2026-02
  known 2025-12-01
  jobs + [bolt] lives 2025-01-01..2026-02-28
  salary[bolt, *] = 100
ask q: sal_at[bolt, 2026-03, 2026-04-15], sal_at[bolt, 2026-03, 2026-02-15], sal_at[bolt, 2026-02, 2026-04-15]
ask q2: salary[bolt, 2026-03]
=== expect
q: (none, none, 100.00 PLN)
  cut 2026-12-31
q2: none
  cut 2026-12-31
